# Line-ending policy (design spec §6.7).
#
# Tree checksums are computed over committed bytes with no normalisation, so
# LF -> CRLF is a real change and MUST alter the checksum. Cross-platform
# stability therefore has to come from checkout policy, not from the checksum.
#
# General sources and docs: normalise, so collaboration across platforms is sane.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Byte-stable assets: never transformed on checkout, whatever the platform.
fixtures/**  -text
*.patch      -text
